  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Using Unity 2019.4.29f1 and SDK3 2021.08.04.11.23.\nThe avatar descriptor editor seems to cause an import loop of sorts under certain conditions, seemingly because of viewpoint editing. \nI've found 2 ways to reproduce in a new project with only the SDK imported.\nFirst way:\n- Create an empty game object.\n- Drag it into assets to create a prefab.\n- Right click the prefab in the hierarchy and 'Open in Prefab mode'\n- Add an avatar descriptor and click edit on the viewpoint field.\n- Object gets marked dirty, get saved and seemingly reimported and it loops forever until you click onto another object or minimize the avatar descriptor script so it's editor stops drawing.\n- Your avatar descriptor editor is now cursed and will do this every time it's drawn, regardless of mode.\nSecond way:\n- Create an empty game object.\n- Add an avatar descriptor to it\n- Click 'Edit' on the viewpoint field.\n- Drag your game object into assets to create a prefab with viewpoint edit mode still active.\n- Your descriptor is now cursed.",
